# Stitch Design

<!-- Harness scaffold: integration=stitch -->
<!-- Authoring required when team adopts stitch. Mirror the structure of figma-design or claude-design skills. -->

Authoritative knowledge for the `ux-agent` when the project's design integration is **stitch**. Stitch ships an MCP server (`mcp__stitch__*`) — programmatic design generation.

## Inputs

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docs/design/schema.json` | Workspace pointer — `designSystem.{fileKey,url}` carries stitch `project_id` and project URL |
| `docs/features/<id>/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Screen inventory | Authoritative screen list |
| `CLAUDE.md` + `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md` | Form-factor mapping |

## Outputs

| Path | Mutation |
|---|---|
| `docs/features/<id>/DESIGN.md` | Created / replaced — screens table linking to stitch screens |
| `docs/features/<id>/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec | One-line pointer to DESIGN.md |
| `docs/design/schema.json` | Project / screen ids appended |
| `docs/features/<id>/state.json` | `design`, `design_artifact`, `design_provider = "stitch"` |

## Known Stitch MCP tools

- `mcp__stitch__list_projects` — discover available projects
- `mcp__stitch__get_project` — fetch project metadata + design system
- `mcp__stitch__create_project` — create new project (rare; usually use existing)
- `mcp__stitch__list_screens` — enumerate screens in project
- `mcp__stitch__get_screen` — fetch screen content + shareable URL
- `mcp__stitch__generate_screen_from_text` — generate new screen from a prompt
- `mcp__stitch__edit_screens` — modify existing screens
- `mcp__stitch__generate_variants` — produce form-factor variants of a screen
- `mcp__stitch__list_design_systems` / `create_design_system` / `update_design_system` / `apply_design_system` — design system management
- `mcp__stitch__create_design_system_from_design_md` / `upload_design_md` — bootstrap design system from a `design.md` description

